/// Loomfield & Field LLC: a Seattle design agency with about 30 clients, owned 60/40
/// by two partners, two employees, one 1099 illustrator and three company cards.
/// January to June 2026.
///
/// Written against LANGUAGE v4 the way a careful user would. Not runnable.
/// Marks in comments, each explained in FINDINGS.md under the same number:
///   ✗ cannot say: what I needed, and what I wrote instead
///   ✎ says it badly
///   ? the spec is unclear or contradicts itself
///   ⇄ what sync would need to write the line with no typing
/// `▸` is what Axiom would infer or derive, as in the v4 sketch.
base USD
use us
use us/wa                       // B&O tax, retail sales tax on advertising services, PFML, WA Cares
use us/partnership              // ✗ 01a1: no such system yet, and the language cannot write it (see below)

/// Ines Moreau, who keeps this book. `me` is her.
entity me : person
  born    1987-09-02
  filing  single
  lives   us/wa/seattle

/// Theo Okafor, her partner in the agency, 40%.
entity theo : person
  born    1985-02-19
  filing  single
  lives   us/wa/seattle

kind llc : entity
  taxed   partnership            // ▸ its profit reaches the partners' returns, in shares (§4 does not say how)

/// The agency. Accrual books, so that an invoice is income the day it is sent
/// and a write-off means something.
entity loomfield : llc
  owner   me                     // ✗ 01a1: 60% me, 40% theo. `owner` takes one entity (§4), so Theo owns nothing here.
  books   accrual                // ? 01c1: `books` is in §7's text but not in §4's property table
  lives   us/wa/seattle          // ▸ WA laws govern it: B&O, sales tax, payroll

// What the agency's money is for. std has `income` and `spending`; these are the leaves this book needs.
purpose design            : income
purpose retainer          : design
purpose print-production  : income
purpose reimbursed-costs  : income          // ✎ 01b1: a cost re-billed at cost is income and spending at once
purpose late-fees         : income
purpose bad-debt          : spending
purpose contract-labor    : spending
purpose software          : spending
purpose rent              : spending
purpose payroll-tax       : spending
purpose b-and-o           : spending
purpose distribution                        // ✗ 01a2: an owner-to-owner flow is neither income nor spending: a fourth root?
purpose sales-tax-collected                 // ✗ 01a3: nor is this: money passing through, owed to the state
purpose withholding                         //          nor this
purpose accounting        : spending
purpose office            : spending
purpose travel            : spending
purpose meals             : spending
purpose marketing         : spending
purpose fees              : spending

kind accountant  : org
  purpose accounting
kind insurer     : org
  purpose insurance                         // ✎ 01b7: premiums out, claim payouts in; one purpose serves one direction
kind airline     : merchant
  purpose travel
kind rideshare   : merchant
  purpose travel
kind processor-balance : asset               // what a processor holds for you until it pays out
